  "verdictNoLockReason": "Without the lock the jumps shrink to 0.07-0.09 m and the hold stills (0.006-0.015 m, passing), but stance-phase slide medians stay 0.10-0.22 m (5-11x over 0.02) on all three rigs, so no rig clears every bar. The generator input passes the absolute bars (source medians 0.012-0.014 m); the retarget does not preserve it.",
  "defectLocalization": "Two independent bind defects, both rig-independent in signature: (1) the bake-time foot lock (stage lines ~582-657) injects ~1 m single-frame toe jumps at decel onset (frame 66 R / frame 49 L physician) and drags hold feet; with the lock off the same frames show 0.07-0.09 m. (2) a base-bind vertical collapse unrelated to the lock: physician root 0.93->0.51 m and child root 0.66->-0.01 m with toes ending at -0.36/-0.63 m (below floor) on lock AND nolock alike, while the source stays upright (Hips z 0.92-1.00 child) and the nurse stays up (toes 0.02). hipHeightRatio: physician 0.945, nurse 0.974, child 0.665.",
  "followUp": "Card: bake-time foot lock vs kept root motion in motion_bind_from_positions_stage.py (~582-657). Symptom measured: with --foot-contacts and no --strip-horizontal-root-motion, contact-labeled frames get their world XZ pinned while the root keeps advancing, then release in a single-frame jump (0.99 m physician R toe frame 66; 0.94 m L toe frame 49); hold feet travel 0.09-0.29 m. Without the lock: 0.07-0.09 m jumps, 0.006-0.015 m hold. Second card: per-rig vertical collapse (physician/child sink, nurse does not) despite upright source.",
